 **Python exact-version contract.** For requirements declarations, PEP 621 project dependencies and optional dependencies, embedded pip declarations, and Pipfile version fields, a supported valid version constraint is exact only when its parsed specifier contains one non-wildcard `==` version clause. A valid PEP 440 version may contain local, pre-release, post-release, development-release, or epoch components. Poetry dependency version fields also accept a valid bare PEP 440 version as exact, in addition to the same single `==` form. Ranges, wildcard/prefix matching, unversioned declarations, URL/VCS/path dependencies, unsupported syntax, arbitrary equality (`===`), and multiple distinct clauses are not accepted as exact by this bounded static contract. Preserve each format's grammar; do not treat a bare requirements or Pipfile version as a Poetry version field.
 
 Exact means a version constraint, not identity of a build, wheel, index, platform, or file hash. A public `==` pin does not distinguish local variants unless a local label is explicitly included. Extras and markers do not remove an otherwise exact version constraint, but this audit does not claim the same installation on every platform or resolve transitive dependencies.
+
+**Bounded ordinary requirements inline comments (R07-C D-C).** Only the existing requirements graph's ordinary-line route gains the following fallback, using text already captured by its existing body read. Classify the original stripped physical line first: blank/full-line comments, existing include recognition, and existing directive or literal `" @ "` exclusions retain their routes. Never remove a comment before choosing these routes. For an ordinary line, retain any successful parse of the complete original line unchanged, including previously accepted marker or URL forms.
+
+Only when that original ordinary-line parse fails may the fallback apply. If any physical line in this captured file's `text.splitlines()`, after `rstrip()`, ends with a backslash (`\`), disable the added fallback for the entire file. This intentionally conservative veto includes full-line comments, doubled backslashes and later physical lines; it does not interpret escaping or join continuations. It never revokes pre-existing successful parses or changes existing includes, and it does not extend to other captured files.
+
+Otherwise locate only the first ASCII SPACE or TAB immediately followed by `#` in the original stripped line. Strip the prefix before that delimiter and accept it only when the existing `packaging.requirements.Requirement` parser accepts it and its `url` is `None`. A missing delimiter, invalid prefix or URL prefix retains the original full-line failure and diagnostic; do not try a later delimiter or truncate failed diagnostic text. Other Unicode whitespace does not create a delimiter. Preserve original physical source path/line, declaration ordering, canonicalization, specifier and exact-version rules. A newly accepted line emits its declaration instead of its former unsupported-line event.
+
+Recompute closure qualification and package membership from the same existing graph and newly captured declarations under the complete exact requirements contract. Preserve exact/qualified credit and the priorities in §§12.3.3–12.3.8. Newly captured exact declarations may precede existing SKIP branches; newly captured nonexact critical declarations may create package use. Dependency profile detection and init consumers receive the same updated inventory. This can change findings, diagnostics, profiles, generated manifests and exit codes in either direction under the existing thresholds; it adds no new status, severity or persisted field.
+
+This subset applies only to graph requirements lines, not to shared requirement-string parsing for other declaration formats. It does not add reads, candidates, roots, include syntax or edges, depth budget, constraints, editable/VCS/URL support, environment interpolation, continuation processing or manager execution. It is not full pip grammar compatibility: original literal `" @ "` exclusions remain, and a first delimiter inside a quoted marker is not skipped in search of an outer comment. Existing successful whole-line marker parses still take priority.
 
 **Complete exact requirements closure.** Evaluate each discovered `requirements*.txt` root from its actual supported `-r` / `--requirement` include edges, relative to the containing file's directory, after normalization and root-containment checks. Allow normalized internal `..`; reject absolute or escaping targets before reading. A qualifying closure has at least one valid package declaration, every reachable package declaration meets the Python exact-version contract, and every include edge is resolved. Cycles, depth-limit exhaustion, unreadable/missing/escaping files, malformed declarations, and unsupported directives prevent that root from qualifying. Blank lines and comments do not count as declarations. Repeated/shared nodes are deduplicated and are not cycles unless encountered on the active recursion stack. The lock's package set contains only declarations actually reachable from that root, never an unreferenced sibling. Use one graph/result for qualification and package membership. This retains L0 repository aggregation and is independent of the format-lock association contract above.
 
